WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.001
♪♪

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.461
(Food sizzles)

00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:03.503
(Typing on keyboard)

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.590
♪♪

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.092
Neil Cross:
In common with the rest of the
world,

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:13.096
Covid was profoundly disruptive
to this show.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:17.142
Neil Cross:
We were in Mexico City,
filming episode 5,

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:19.144
Neil Cross:
when things got really bad.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:23.690
And we had no idea if it was
gonna be possible 

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.235
Neil Cross:
to film the rest of the show.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:29.029
Neil Cross:
One of our principal characters
is a teenage boy.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.575
And I was terrified that by the
time we got to re-man in 2022,
Charlie would be

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.119
Neil Cross:
6'5", with uh, a lumberjack
beard.

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:40.165
We're very lucky that we figured
out a clever way to come back to
shooting,

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.125
Melissa George:
In a bubble, in the safest way
possible.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.170
Neil Cross:
We picked it up in Guadalajara,
five months later.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.297
This isn't how it's supposed to
be.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.633
I know, but it is what it is.

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:52.010
Neil Cross:
I'd always wanted to have a
story where 

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.513
two characters have
to cross the city on foot
against time.

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:56.098
Neil Cross:
I just wanted to write
a thrilling chase.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:59.017
Neil Cross:
But with the kids I want to do
something a bit different.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.687
Mexico City is the most
fantastic city.

00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:05.315
Neil Cross:
And it's that kind of what do
you get to do

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:08.944
Neil Cross:
when you're a teenager in a city
like that and your parents are gone.

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:10.862
I've never been to Mexico
before.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:12.531
Gabriel Bateman:
It was a culture shock at first.

00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:15.742
I've been trying to learn
Spanish, which has been kind of
hard, but it's been fun.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.537
Do you like chocolate?

00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:22.416
Gabriel is, he's just hilarious
because he, he really does
have that energy

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:23.417
Justin Theroux:
of a fourteen year old boy.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:27.129
He has energy to expend,
he's constantly, you know,
picking at things.

00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:32.884
Justin:
And obviously the way Charlie
is written is, he doesn't want to see flaws in his father.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:35.721
Dina, by contrast, sees 
nothing but flaws.

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:37.806
Neil Cross:
She does not wanna be like
Allie.

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.808
Dina's tragedy is that she is
Allie.

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:45.439
I think she yearns for that
normal life so she can just get
a sense of what it's like

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.065
Logan Polish:
outside of her dad.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.567
Dina:
Charlie, you don't want that.
-Huh

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.152
(All talking)

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:52.279
Dina:
You bourgeois, hipster
dilettantes...

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:53.363
Okay okay.

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.448
Come on.

00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:57.367
Gabriel Bateman:
Logan and I have a great banter
that we started at the beginning

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.578
Gabriel Bateman:
and we have a really close bond,
so I thinks it's nice

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:01.455
Gabriel Bateman:
to have someone to hang out with
on and off set.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:04.875
Uh and that really comes off as
like a sibling dynamic onscreen.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.585
You can't.
-This is fun.

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:10.172
I wanted to write a story for
a young American man

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:13.216
Neil Cross:
where we see a boy on the cusp
of manhood.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:18.513
Charlie has very skewed ideas
about what it is to be a man.

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:24.478
Neil Cross:
And I'm very interested in that
fearful desire to be able to 

00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:27.272
Neil Cross:
prove one's masculinity through
violence.

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:32.944
Neil Cross:
We see a crucial moment in the
real beginning of Charlie's journey.

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:33.945
Neil Cross:
The kid's got a gun.

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:37.657
♪♪

